Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 27 AVPs from 3GPP TS 29.329
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3GPP TS 29.329 V19.1.0 defines these AVPs in vendor 10415, which the
dictionary has no entry for at their codes:

  Call-Reference-Info (720): Grouped, 2 members, clause 6.3.29
  Call-Reference-Number (721): OctetString, clause 6.3.30
  AS-Number (722): OctetString, clause 6.3.31
  Any-User-Indication (723): Enumerated, 2 values, clause 8.3.1
  Subscription-Identity (724): UTF8String, clause 8.3.2
  Notification-Address (725): UTF8String, clause 8.3.3
  Notification-Correlation-Identity (726): UTF8String, clause 8.3.4
  Event-Reporting-Options (727): Grouped, 6 members, clause 8.3.5
  Report-Mode (728): Enumerated, 2 values, clause 8.3.6
  One-Time-Report (729): Enumerated, 2 values, clause 8.3.7
  Max-Number-of-Reports (730): Unsigned32, clause 8.3.8
  Report-Period (731): Unsigned32, clause 8.3.9
  Event-List (732): Grouped, 3 members, clause 8.3.10
  Ims-Event (733): Enumerated, 5 values, clause 8.3.11
  Ims-Event-Filter (734): Grouped, 4 members, clause 8.3.12
  Ims-Event-Report (735): Grouped, 3 members, clause 8.3.13
  Ims-Event-Report-Information (736): Grouped, 2 members, clause 8.3.14
  Adc-Report (737): Enumerated, 3 values, clause 8.3.15
  Bdc-Report (738): Enumerated, 2 values, clause 8.3.16
  Session-Identity (739): UTF8String, clause 8.3.17
  Timestamp (740): Time, clause 8.3.18
  App-Bind-Information (741): Grouped, 2 members, clause 8.3.19
  App-Dc-Information (742): Grouped, 2 members, clause 8.3.20
  Application-Identity (743): UTF8String, clause 8.3.21
  Stream-Identity (744): UTF8String, clause 8.3.22
  Adc-Endpoint-Type (745): Enumerated, 2 values, clause 8.3.23
  Calling-Identity (746): UTF8String, clause 8.3.24

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Not added here: Called-Identity, code 747, named like the dictionary's
code 3916 of vendor 10415. Wireshark names each display filter field
after its AVP, so two entries named alike need one renamed, as
Cx-User-Data and Sh-User-Data are.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
